43 0 obj<</Type/Annot/Rect[51.4 70.8 264.6 213.8]/Subtype/FreeText/M(D:20260213162429Z00'00')/T<>/Contents(First- hand observations living in Germany.\nPrevious experience working in the field of Facility Management.\nClose contact with industry experts for technical and stratergy validation.\nInsight into the "washing vs. cleaning" market gap allows me to address the specific failure of touchless spray drones in removing heavy urban soot, positioning the venture to meet the high standards of facility managers in the DACH region.)/NM(Zotero-7J49KRRA)/Zotero:Key(7J49KRRA)/Zotero:AuthorName<>/Zotero:Rect[51.4 70.8 264.6 213.8]/Zotero:Rotation 0/Zotero:FontSize 10/Zotero:Color[0 0 0]/DA(/Helvetica 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg)/F 4/CA 1/Border[0 0 1]>>endobj
44 0 obj<</Type/Annot/Rect[58 525.2 559.8 603.2]/Subtype/FreeText/M(D:20260213162245Z00'00')/T<>/Contents(The facade cleaning industry is largely outdated that are highly labour intensive and risky. While other drone cleaning solutions focus on "touchless" spray drones, that are ineffective to clean heavy dirt and use excess water.\nOur insight is that a drone must be a "Flying Floor Scrubber" \(contact\) to be sustainable and effective. Furthermore, we realize that cleaning is the perfect moment to perform an Maintenance Audit using thermal mapping.)/NM(Zotero-RPWBSWNJ)/Zotero:Key(RPWBSWNJ)/Zotero:AuthorName<>/Zotero:Rect[58 525.2 559.8 603.2]/Zotero:Rotation 0/Zotero:FontSize 10/Zotero:Color[0 0 0]/DA(/Helvetica 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg)/F 4/CA 1/Border[0 0 1]>>endobj
45 0 obj<</Type/Annot/Rect[332.5 83.2 564.9 213.2]/Subtype/FreeText/M(D:20260213162448Z00'00')/T<>/Contents(We are driven by safety and sustainability. We want to eliminate the risk of human workers hanging from ropes at heights. We want to replace a "dumb" maintenance task into a smart, data-driven process.\n\nMaturization of stabilization a drone while it scrubs a wall presents a rare chance to solve a tangible industrial problem through advanced engineering.)/NM(Zotero-K4MMTLM6)/Zotero:Key(K4MMTLM6)/Zotero:AuthorName<>/Zotero:Rect[332.5 83.2 564.9 213.2]/Zotero:Rotation 0/Zotero:FontSize 10/Zotero:Color[0 0 0]/DA(/Helvetica 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg)/F 4/CA 1/Border[0 0 1]>>endobj
